// Installed Shortcut name: UTIL - Jelly Format Greeting
// Purpose: Format one name as greeting Text; default to Friend without input.
// Role: Example reusable utility
// Specification revision: 1 | Interface version: 1.0
// Input: Optional single Text; missing/empty uses Friend; whitespace preserved.
// Output: One Text value, Hello, <name>!, with no added newline.
// Direct execution: Default greeting via no-recipient Respond; no input prompt.
// Called execution: Returns greeting to Run Shortcut; no intended extra display.
// Errors: No type validation/catch; action failure or cancellation may halt.
// Unsupported: Lists/non-Text; Share Sheet/Siri/background contexts not specified.
// Dependencies: None | External apps/services: None
// Side effects: Respond when no recipient; no files/network/clipboard changes.
// Permissions: No protected data access required by these actions.
// Target: iOS 26 provisional; actual device and Jellycuts app version unknown.
// Candidate compiler: Open-Jellycore e1ec31c2ee192c8721749f9eb3b50108e38891cf
// Evidence: Syntax reviewed against docs/source; not compiled/imported/tested.
// References: ../docs/jellycuts-reference.md | Tests: ../tests/examples.md

import Shortcuts

var name = "Friend"
if ShortcutInput != nil {
    name = ShortcutInput
}

text(text: "Hello, ${name}!") >> greeting
output(result: "${greeting}", noResultBehavior: Respond, response: "${greeting}")
